.DS_Store
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/sdks
!.yarn/versions
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo
.build/

dsh-plugin-desktop/dist/
dsh-plugin-desktop/lib/
dsh-community-market/lib/
dsh-company-skills/lib/

.env.yarn
.deloitte-ca-bundle.pem
.pi/

# Deterministic rebuild outputs, never committed (issue #011): the skills
# bundle is rebuilt byte-identically from dsh-company-skills/skills/ by
# `node dsh-company-skills/scripts/build-bundle-asset.mjs` (run by the
# workspace `check` and by the CI pre-pack step, which also copies it into
# plugin-sources staging trees — see .github/workflows/company-catalog-*.yml
# and tools/company-catalog/ensure-skills-bundles.mjs).
dsh-company-skills/assets/skills.bundle
tools/company-catalog/plugin-sources/*/assets/skills.bundle
# Transitional rule (#011 review): the two legacy v1-era staging pins below
# stay COMMITTED until their catalog entries are revoked→retired — they are
# md5-pinned to the PUBLISHED 0.1.0/0.1.1 tgz bytes, so a fresh CI checkout
# must repack from exactly these bytes or the publish-local tarball byte gate
# blocks every beta publish (0.1.0/0.1.1 shipped v1-only decoders, so a
# v2-rebuilt drift would be semantically broken too). From 0.1.2 on, staging
# bundles are CI-reproduced (ensure-skills-bundles) and never committed.
!tools/company-catalog/plugin-sources/dsh-company-skills-0.1.0/assets/skills.bundle
!tools/company-catalog/plugin-sources/dsh-company-skills-0.1.1/assets/skills.bundle
# The .bundle-rebuilt marker ensure-skills-bundles drops into each staging
# tree it provisioned (measure.mjs re-measures those entries' treeDigest
# from the CI-packed bytes; never committed, never packed into a tgz).
tools/company-catalog/plugin-sources/*/.bundle-rebuilt